WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:02.931
Film Courage: I was reading that a high school
journalism teacher was trying to help her

00:00:02.931 --> 00:00:07.500
students decipher Tweets and fake news and
that’s something that five years ago, we

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:09.330
wouldn’t even be having this conversation.

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:14.639
Dr. Ken Atchity, Producer: I have a really
strange theory about this whole thing about

00:00:14.639 --> 00:00:24.240
fake news is that…I don’t even know how
to say this because…I think the head honcho

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:32.450
is kind of a break through cultural character
I don’t have any fond feelings for him and

00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:34.530
I could go on and on about that.

00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:38.270
But he is an eccentric creative person.

00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:45.629
He is the most amazing producer I’ve ever
seen in my life and I can’t even imagine

00:00:45.629 --> 00:00:48.420
one more powerful than he is.

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:54.630
A few years ago people around the world didn’t
even know who he was.

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:58.770
People in New York new who he was but mostly
in a negative way.

00:00:58.770 --> 00:01:03.679
But in today’s world whether you are in
Thailand like I was a few weeks ago or whether

00:01:03.679 --> 00:01:11.860
you were in an island off the coast of Samoa
or in Latvia or Estonia or Alabania, you can’t

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:15.610
pick up a paper that doesn’t have the word
“Big Guy” in it.

00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:26.409
And his ability to get the media to do what
he wants them to do is almost infinite, it’s

00:01:26.409 --> 00:01:27.850
astonishing.

00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:30.060
People say “Well he is a liar.”

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:34.649
But the more I hear that over the last few
years the more I start thinking what is really

00:01:34.649 --> 00:01:42.969
going on (my wife would hurt me for saying
this) is that he is changing or awakening

00:01:42.969 --> 00:01:49.500
us to our strange views of truth.

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:54.869
Because I don’t think he knows this (I don’t
think it’s conscious on his part) but he

00:01:54.869 --> 00:02:02.520
instinctively knows that truth is completely
relative.

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:07.810
And if a society decides that it’s not relative
then that is a social decision.

00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:13.530
Just like the continent of reasoning saying
“We are going to agree that this is true.”

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:18.610
But he’s saying whatever is true…the only
thing that is true is whatever I am saying

00:02:18.610 --> 00:02:24.470
at the moment and that’s the way I look
at it (it’s true) and he’s got a lot of

00:02:24.470 --> 00:02:29.050
people that even though some of it sounds
just plain crazy.

00:02:29.050 --> 00:02:34.230
But isn’t that the way creative people always
sound at the beginning?

00:02:34.230 --> 00:02:41.960
So I’m afraid and kind of excited that we
may be going into a whole new era of post-truth

00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:44.210
era.

00:02:44.210 --> 00:02:50.660
And no one ever quite answered Pilot’s question
that he asked 2,000 years go “What is truth?”

00:02:50.660 --> 00:02:56.620
But I think the world of the head honcho is
a world that is getting closer to answering

00:02:56.620 --> 00:03:01.900
that then we’ve ever been before because
what is we decide to just dispense with the

00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:04.420
concept of truth?

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:11.780
A lot of things wold change, but they are
already changing because of him and I think

00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:17.090
it’s a very strange and troubling situation.

00:03:17.090 --> 00:03:21.560
But it’s also kind of exhilarating because
maybe it’s time that we do have a different

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:26.950
view of what truth is and maybe we can learn
something from the whole thing.

00:03:26.950 --> 00:03:30.590
So I don’t know if this has anything to
do with our interview but…

00:03:30.590 --> 00:03:36.290
Film Courage: Well if we look at writing and
fake news, if we look at [William] Randolph

00:03:36.290 --> 00:03:42.570
Hearst, he would stage different events back
in the day where a woman would faint on the

00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:48.840
street and they would write about it and it
was part of just generating content.

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:53.290
The thing is we didn’t have the Internet
back then so news would spread as fast and

00:03:53.290 --> 00:03:58.340
it wouldn’t create chaos in other countries
and our own and then it turns out it’s not

00:03:58.340 --> 00:03:59.340
even true.

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:04.730
Dr. Atchity: Well when we look at what’s
happened here, the American people decided

00:04:04.730 --> 00:04:07.500
with their votes one way or the other.

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:10.850
I mean I know it was the electoral college
not the popular vote.

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:20.650
But a lot of Americans voted for a reality
show over somebody who was just a little too

00:04:20.650 --> 00:04:26.740
truthful or whatever a little too logical,
a little too much of the continent of reasons.

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:31.780
But they voted for the most entertaining of
the two characters.

00:04:31.780 --> 00:04:34.510
They voted for entertainment basically.

00:04:34.510 --> 00:04:35.510
And that’s scary.

00:04:35.510 --> 00:04:40.311
I mean ultimately these other actors are talking
about running and some of them already have

00:04:40.311 --> 00:04:44.140
run and actresses, etc.

00:04:44.140 --> 00:04:52.230
The blurring of politics and entertainment
is very dangerous but what if it changes the

00:04:52.230 --> 00:04:53.230
world.

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:57.050
But what if it change the world for not only
the worst but changes it for the better.

00:04:57.050 --> 00:05:03.370
I mean what is an enlightened guy like George
Clooney becomes president.

00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:04.370
Film Courage: That would be nice.

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:06.430
Dr. Atchity: And he gets elected because he
is George Clooney.

00:05:06.430 --> 00:05:09.480
He gets elected because he’s an entertainer.

00:05:09.480 --> 00:05:13.050
What is a guy like Ronald Reagan becomes president?

00:05:13.050 --> 00:05:15.080
Film Courage: He was The Great Communicator
though.

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:19.050
Dr. Atchity: Yes, well he was a great actor,
great communicator.

00:05:19.050 --> 00:05:24.370
He didn’t need to write his lines, he knew
how to deliver his lines.

00:05:24.370 --> 00:05:30.510
So I think all of that is very interesting
and it’s about how the creative worlds intertwine

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:39.720
with daily existence and you watch the broadcasters
and I try to watch Fox news once and awhile

00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:42.620
and I find it very difficult to watch it.

00:05:42.620 --> 00:05:48.820
But then when I come back to watch CNN and
MSNBC I realize they must find…I understand

00:05:48.820 --> 00:05:57.620
how they feel that is hard to watch because
both sides of the coin are manipulating views

00:05:57.620 --> 00:06:01.710
of reality to get messages across.

00:06:01.710 --> 00:06:03.220
And that’s what writing is about.

00:06:03.220 --> 00:06:05.630
Isn’t that what creativity is all about?

00:06:05.630 --> 00:06:10.300
A painter paints something like Rothberg,
who would have thought you could have painted

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:13.940
a painting with no figures in it at all (just
color)?

00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:17.310
And that’s the world we are going through.

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:23.330
So it’s kind of like we’re on another
frontier of the human’s mind’s evolution

00:06:23.330 --> 00:06:26.560
and we’ll see what happens from it.

00:06:26.560 --> 00:06:33.650
I’m afraid that certain things are going
to be gone for good after this presidency.

00:06:33.650 --> 00:06:41.960
We may not ever get any candidate who isn’t
a visionary in one way or another.

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:46.810
And the big cheese is a visionary even if
you think his vision is dark, clearly he is

00:06:46.810 --> 00:06:47.810
a visionary.

00:06:47.810 --> 00:06:52.350
He doesn’t like the way things are and he’s
trying to break them up.

00:06:52.350 --> 00:06:56.460
And only when things are broken up can they
be put back together again.

00:06:56.460 --> 00:07:02.780
So he’s a spoiler and the world…history
is filled with spoilers.

00:07:02.780 --> 00:07:10.080
And huge catastrophes and huge changes for
the better have occurred because of spoilers

00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:11.630
and who knows where it’s going.

00:07:11.630 --> 00:07:19.419
But I think it’s interesting that the entertainment
world being mixed with the world of reality,

00:07:19.419 --> 00:07:21.520
it’s going to make it much more challenging.

00:07:21.520 --> 00:07:26.639
And I think the Internet is largely responsible
for that because the first thing if you have

00:07:26.639 --> 00:07:30.510
a certain medical condition you instantly
Google.

00:07:30.510 --> 00:07:34.460
And the first thing you read you go “Oh
my Gosh!”

00:07:34.460 --> 00:07:39.810
I’m going to die or I’m goin to die in
this really bizarre way.

00:07:39.810 --> 00:07:44.070
And then you read something else that makes
it look like everybody has this problem and

00:07:44.070 --> 00:07:45.680
that it’s not a big issue.

00:07:45.680 --> 00:07:51.780
And then you keep reading and you get more
and more confused and you go “Wait a minute?

00:07:51.780 --> 00:07:53.520
This isn’t making sense.”

00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:57.540
Everything is out there and how do you organize
it?

00:07:57.540 --> 00:08:05.449
And faced with that you are facing the issue
of creativity because the creator is the guy

00:08:05.449 --> 00:08:10.250
or the girl who looks at things and goes “This
whole thing is a mess.

00:08:10.250 --> 00:08:12.910
I’m going to make something spectacular
out of it.

00:08:12.910 --> 00:08:15.770
I’m going to make SENSE out of it.”

00:08:15.770 --> 00:08:20.580
And I think that is why the world is getting
more and more interesting.

00:08:20.580 --> 00:08:24.210
Where it’s going I don’t know?

00:08:24.210 --> 00:08:27.250
But it’s going to be interesting.

